dyld: skip the fairplay mremap_encrypted registration in the dyld2 loader too (aarch64 port)

Patch 0002 excluded the FairPlay `mremap_encrypted` block under DARLING in the dyld3 loader
(dyld3/Loading.cpp), but the guest boots through the dyld2 loader, whose
ImageLoaderMachOCompressed::registerEncryption has the SAME block guarded on `(__arm__ ||
__arm64__) && !TARGET_OS_SIMULATOR`. On an arm64 guest it compiled and called ::mremap_encrypted,
which the emulation does not provide, so every dylib with an LC_ENCRYPTION_INFO command (cryptid
0, i.e. all of them) failed to load with ENOSYS and dyld aborted with 'Library not loaded:
libSystem.B.dylib'. Add `&& !defined(DARLING)` exactly as 0002 did, so the block disappears under
the emulation. cider defines DARLING.
--- a/src/ImageLoaderMachOCompressed.cpp
+++ b/src/ImageLoaderMachOCompressed.cpp
@@ -2125,7 +2125,11 @@
 
 void ImageLoaderMachOCompressed::registerEncryption(const encryption_info_command* encryptCmd, const LinkContext& context)
 {
-#if (__arm__ || __arm64__) && !TARGET_OS_SIMULATOR
+	// cider (aarch64 port): exclude the FairPlay mremap_encrypted registration under Darling, the
+	// same way patch 0002 does for the dyld3 loader (dyld3/Loading.cpp). The emulation has no
+	// FairPlay kernel and does not provide ::mremap_encrypted, so on an arm64 guest this block
+	// otherwise calls it and gets ENOSYS, aborting every dylib load. cider defines DARLING.
+#if (__arm__ || __arm64__) && !TARGET_OS_SIMULATOR && !defined(DARLING)
 	if ( encryptCmd == NULL )
 		return;
 	// fMachOData not set up yet, need to manually find mach_header
